Relevant columns & their potential usage  
• DEATHRECORDS."Icd10Code": join key that links each death record to the ICD‑10 description in ICD10CODE.  
• ICD10CODE."Description": lets us search for the words “discharge” or “vehicle”.  
• DEATHRECORDS."RaceRecode3": numeric race category – code 1 corresponds to “White” in RACERECODE3.  
• RACERECODE3."Code"/"Description": confirms which numeric code means “White”.  
• DEATHRECORDS."AgeRecode27", "AgeRecode12", "AgeRecode52": pre‑built age‑group recodes that can be used for aggregation.  
• AGERECODE27 (and 12 / 52) ."Code"/"Description": readable text for the age‑group codes.  
Typical conditions you may see  
• ICD10CODE."Description" ILIKE '%discharge%'  -- and NOT ILIKE '%urethral discharge%' etc.  
• ICD10CODE."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'  
• DEATHRECORDS."RaceRecode3" = 1               -- White  
• Join DEATHRECORDS."Icd10Code" = ICD10CODE."Code"  
• Group BY age‑group column to get counts; use AVG() if multiple years / sub‑populations.  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that gradually build understanding from simple lookups to an aggregated comparison.  
All column names are enclosed in double quotes.

```sql
-- 1) Description: Inspect some ICD‑10 descriptions that contain the word “discharge”.
SELECT DISTINCT "Code", "Description"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE
WHERE "Description" ILIKE '%discharge%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Same as #1, but explicitly exclude the three phrases we must ignore.
SELECT DISTINCT "Code", "Description"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE
WHERE "Description" ILIKE '%discharge%'
  AND "Description" NOT ILIKE '%urethral discharge%'
  AND "Description" NOT ILIKE '%discharge of firework%'
  AND "Description" NOT ILIKE '%legal intervention involving firearm discharge%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Inspect some ICD‑10 descriptions that contain the word “vehicle”.
SELECT DISTINCT "Code", "Description"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE
WHERE "Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Verify the numeric code that represents “White” in the race‑recode lookup.
SELECT "Code", "Description"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.RACERECODE3
WHERE "Description" ILIKE '%white%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: View a handful of death records for White decedents (race code 1).
SELECT "Id",
       "Icd10Code",
       "AgeRecode27",
       "RaceRecode3"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS
WHERE "RaceRecode3" = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Join death records (White only) with ICD‑10 text and keep those whose
--                 description contains “discharge” (with required exclusions).
SELECT dr."Id",
       dr."AgeRecode27",
       dr."Icd10Code",
       ic."Description"
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS      dr
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE         ic
  ON   dr."Icd10Code" = ic."Code"
WHERE  dr."RaceRecode3" = 1
  AND  ic."Description" ILIKE '%discharge%'
  AND  ic."Description" NOT ILIKE '%urethral discharge%'
  AND  ic."Description" NOT ILIKE '%discharge of firework%'
  AND  ic."Description" NOT ILIKE '%legal intervention involving firearm discharge%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Same style as #6 but for ICD‑10 descriptions containing “vehicle”.
SELECT dr."Id",
       dr."AgeRecode27",
       dr."Icd10Code",
       ic."Description"
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS dr
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE    ic
  ON   dr."Icd10Code" = ic."Code"
WHERE  dr."RaceRecode3" = 1
  AND  ic."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Count deaths by age‑group (AgeRecode27) for the “discharge” set.
SELECT dr."AgeRecode27",
       COUNT(*) AS "death_count_discharge"
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS dr
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE    ic
  ON   dr."Icd10Code" = ic."Code"
WHERE  dr."RaceRecode3" = 1
  AND  ic."Description" ILIKE '%discharge%'
  AND  ic."Description" NOT ILIKE '%urethral discharge%'
  AND  ic."Description" NOT ILIKE '%discharge of firework%'
  AND  ic."Description" NOT ILIKE '%legal intervention involving firearm discharge%'
GROUP  BY dr."AgeRecode27"
ORDER  BY dr."AgeRecode27"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Count deaths by age‑group (AgeRecode27) for the “vehicle” set.
SELECT dr."AgeRecode27",
       COUNT(*) AS "death_count_vehicle"
FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS dr
JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE    ic
  ON   dr."Icd10Code" = ic."Code"
WHERE  dr."RaceRecode3" = 1
  AND  ic."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
GROUP  BY dr."AgeRecode27"
ORDER  BY dr."AgeRecode27"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: Combine the two subtotals and compute the difference in
--                  average deaths per age group (discharge – vehicle).
WITH discharge_ct AS (
    SELECT dr."AgeRecode27",
           COUNT(*)::FLOAT / NULLIF(COUNT(DISTINCT dr."CurrentDataYear"),0) AS "avg_discharge"
    FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS dr
    JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE    ic
      ON   dr."Icd10Code" = ic."Code"
    WHERE  dr."RaceRecode3" = 1
      AND  ic."Description" ILIKE '%discharge%'
      AND  ic."Description" NOT ILIKE '%urethral discharge%'
      AND  ic."Description" NOT ILIKE '%discharge of firework%'
      AND  ic."Description" NOT ILIKE '%legal intervention involving firearm discharge%'
    GROUP  BY dr."AgeRecode27"
),
vehicle_ct AS (
    SELECT dr."AgeRecode27",
           COUNT(*)::FLOAT / NULLIF(COUNT(DISTINCT dr."CurrentDataYear"),0) AS "avg_vehicle"
    FROM   DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS dr
    JOIN   DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE    ic
      ON   dr."Icd10Code" = ic."Code"
    WHERE  dr."RaceRecode3" = 1
      AND  ic."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
    GROUP  BY dr."AgeRecode27"
)
SELECT COALESCE(d."AgeRecode27", v."AgeRecode27")          AS "AgeRecode27",
       d."avg_discharge",
       v."avg_vehicle",
       d."avg_discharge" - v."avg_vehicle"                 AS "avg_difference"
FROM   discharge_ct d
FULL   JOIN vehicle_ct v
  ON   d."AgeRecode27" = v."AgeRecode27"
ORDER  BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

The ten queries progress from simple lookups to a combined computation that can be expanded beyond the 20‑row limit for full analysis.
